d. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.1 to 5.1. December accounts for 16% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 10. Contract [1], for 14,490 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts in December cover the same need and verify if awardee A's contracts repeat the same services. Review contract [1] to see if the amount aligns with standard market rates.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["cs3t0G0mheXkY6rls5tG9A%3D%3D","CzXkvg205kmP%2Bo96UAV7cQ%3D%3D","ASgJW8GrSYrzAq95uGTrDQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}